      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes a lot of sense for the internal dynamics of the group. To really nail the \"true crime\" feel, I want to look at the more controversial side of things—the stuff that actually makes the news. \n\nWhen looking at those specific gang structures you mentioned, like the ones in Chinese or Korean American communities, how do those actually manifest in their criminal methods? I'm trying to understand if there are certain \"traits\" or behavioral patterns that are commonly associated with these specific ethnic crime syndicates in real-world criminal profiling. For instance, is there a specific way they handle recruitment or internal discipline that's distinctively tied to their cultural background, or perhaps certain types of crimes they tend to gravitate toward more than others? I want to make sure the script doesn't just feel like generic crime, but feels like it's reflecting the specific \"flavor\" of these types of organizations.",
